[Music]  the recent arrival of the long-awaited  spider-man no way home was thrilling for  many reasons but the promise of seeing  more than one of spidey's biggest foes  joined the marvel cinematic universe for  the first time arguably had fans more  excited than any other aspect of its  release ever since alfred molina  revealed that he was reprising the role  of dark ark a character he first  portrayed in sam raimi's spider-man 2 in  2004 franchise devotees began to eagerly  anticipate the chance to see he and  various villains from the other  spider-man films take on tom holland's  peter parker jamie foxx's electro is one  of the antagonists from a prior  spider-man movie who made their mcu  debut in no way home electro first  appeared on the big screen in  the amazing spider-man 2. though the  film was considered one of the worst to  start the fame to webslinger elektro was  certainly a memorable villain making his  reintroduction in the latest spider-man  film a welcome inclusion in spite of the  poor reception of his first film  appearance with that said the actor  recently revealed that he initially felt  hesitant to reprise the role prior to  accepting and would only return if one  condition in particular was met first  mcu architect kevin feige and sony  producer amy pascal recently sat down  with brandon davis from comicbook.com  and amidst the discussion of various  other topics related to spider-man no  way home the trio eventually got to  talking about electro when the character  first appeared in the amazing spider-man  2 many fans were upset by the  character's full body spanning electric  blue color which was a far cry from his  look in the comics however trailers for  spider-man no way home revealed that in  his latest film electro would be  outfitted in a costume much more akin to  how the character appeared in his comic  book source material a costume which  also features an iron man arc reactor  this subject came up when davis asked  feige if electro lost his blue  appearance because of that arc reactor  feige a veteran when it comes to  avoiding spoiling his own movies replied  i won't say that you're wrong i also  won't say that you're right he did share  however that the studios promised thugs  that electro wouldn't be blue this time  around fox himself has publicly shared  his distaste for the blue costume  speaking at the cc xp panel he expressed  his enthusiasm for the new take on the  character in the mcu saying he was  excited for the change electro is one of  the more sympathetic spider-man villains  and the comic accurate revision to his  appearance in no way home indicates  marvel's commitment to bringing this  character to life the right way  following the release of spider-man no  way home on december 17th jamie foxx  further discussed returning to the role  of electro in an interview published on  the official marvel website after fox  reiterated that the promise of the  character sporting a new appearance  contributed to him accepting the role he  went on to explain how elektro's  acknowledgment of his new look in the  movie script was integral to pulling off  such a drastic alteration to his  previously established character fox  said the biggest thing that changed is  that he acknowledged the way he looked  he acknowledged oh i like this i dig  this by doing that it answers any  questions like why or what's this thing  being able to do that and just bringing  a little of the way i wanted to talk and  how i wanted to present myself elektro  has a little hipness to him foxx had  further kind things to say about his  character's new look in response to a  question about the fact that his updated  costume resembles an electrician's  uniform it's electrician chic what i'm  saying is that it's fly it's not a cape  or anything like that i really dug that  that's cool because it keeps it  practical practical magic is what you  could call it because he's so practical  so while he appears to have disliked the  look of the character the first time  around fox offered nothing but praise  for both the process through which the  character was redesigned and the  appearance they ultimately landed on  during the production of no way home  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  no way home are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  you

